    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>International Institute for Population Sciences (IIPS) for the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare: National Family Health Survey, rounds 4 (2015-16) and 5 (2019-21), state and national fact sheets. Retrieved from MoSPI's eSankhyiki API (nfhs/getNfhsRecords), vintage <b id="prov-vintage">{round5.vintage}</b>; the raw dump is data/raw/nfhs-records.json. Checked against the DHS Program's tabulation of the same surveys (data/raw/nfhs-dhs-crosscheck.json) and the NFHS-5 national report.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and uncertainty</h6>
        <p>Survey estimates are final on release; the fact sheets publish no confidence intervals, and the national report's sampling-error tables are the place to look. A state estimate rests on a few thousand households; a small union territory's on far fewer. Figures in brackets (an asterisk here) rest on 25 to 49 people.</p>
